{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/573032-supercharging-embeds","id":573032,"title":"Supercharging Embeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T12:47:53-07:00","id":573032,"title":"Supercharging Embeds","content":"What does supercharging an embed do? It's mentioned that it powers up an embed by flowing Aether through it, But to what effect can supercharging an embed like Ellipses do anything like the exploit Stop? In the example Wendy uses No Quarter to force fight to the death and gives the fighters superhuman strength, and removes the pain response from their bodies and the ST gives them fangs and says that while they won't seek victims they will kill anyone they see.<br /> <br /> What does this mean? Is the strength and fangs just narrative or do they actually add dice and lethal fangs? Does the lack of pain response prevent wound penalties? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:32:51-07:00","id":573795,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with the question. Are you referring to the difference between Embeds and Exploits? Because &quot;supercharging&quot; an Embed is the rationale behind how Exploits work in the game - you take an Embed, supercharge it with aether, and it results in an Exploit? By nature, Embeds <i>can't</i> have aether expenditures. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD p158</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Exploit relies on a demon\u2019s knowledge of the world\u2019s metaphysical subroutines, just like Embeds, but instead of gently applying this knowledge, the demon forces Aether into the system, overcharging it and directing the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or are you referring to overclocking gadgets instead? Is this something from the Translation Guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T06:58:51-07:00","id":573883,"title":"","content":"The OP is asking about the demonblooded ability to supercharge embeds to exploit levels.<br /> <br /> Now as to answer the question, a supercharged embed can pretty much do whatever the ST is okay with it doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-30-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T19:20:58-08:00","id":1435935,"title":"","content":"I would have the embed go massively overboard, for example. Check backdrop could make people not fire at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T17:08:17-08:00","id":1436476,"title":"","content":"As STsword said, it's a demon blooded trying to mimic how demons and up an embed to an exploit but unlike a demon they dont have the consistency. This means that each time they attempt such, it's a risk and even when it works as they want it it likely won't be exactly as they want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}